414 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Test of between-subjects effects show that neither learning style nor note-taking had a statistically significant influence on comprehension or memory recall. Learning style showed non-significant results for comprehension, F\(2,30\) = 1.861, p = 0.170, partial eta-squared = 0.111 \(medium effect\), and for memory recall, F\(2,30\) = 0.489, p = 0.618, partial eta-squared = 0.032 \(small effect\), while note-taking also produced non-significant effects for comprehension, F\(1,30\) = 0.170, p = 0.683, partial eta-squared = 0.006, and memory recall, F\(1,30\) = 1.204, p = 0.281, partial eta-squared = 0.039. Overall, although some effect sizes fall within the small to medium range, these were not strong enough to reach statistical significance, indicating that students performed similarly regardless of learning style or note-taking condition.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
